 "post": {
  "title": "He Tapped Happy Birthday. Nobody Got It #shorts",
  "description": "Otto taps a song on his desk and can't believe Lila misses it. In 1990 Stanford psychology student Elizabeth Newton had people tap out well-known songs: tappers predicted listeners would name half of them, but of 120 songs listeners named just 3 (2.5%). It's called the curse of knowledge: once you know something, you can't imagine not knowing it. #psychology #shorts #communication",
